course: dictionary
lesson: 4758
title: Hourly: every hour, or per hour
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Hourly is a time word. Its simplest meaning is every hour, or once an hour. A bus that runs hourly comes once every hour, so you never wait longer than that for the next one.
explain: Hourly also means by the hour. «A salary is yearly pay; an hourly rate is pay for each hour worked; a career is the work someone does over their life.» Here, a salary is paid over a whole year, but an hourly rate is paid for each single hour. Words like salary, career and hourly all describe pay or work, but over different lengths of time.
explain: To find a total from an hourly rate, multiply the rate by the number of hours. If you earn £6 an hour for 5 hours, that is 6 × 5 = £30. Clue words such as each, per and for every tell you that hourly means per hour.
fact: Hourly means happening every hour, or once an hour.
fact: Hourly also means counted or paid by the hour, as in an hourly wage.
fact: An «hourly rate» is the pay for each hour worked.
fact: «Salary» means yearly pay, so a salary is not hourly.
fact: As an adverb, hourly can mean very often, any time now, as in «expected hourly».
exercise: «An hourly rate is pay for each hour worked.» What does hourly rate mean? | Pay for each year worked | Pay once at the end of a career | *Pay for each hour worked | Pay only on Sundays
exercise: A bus runs hourly. How often does it run? | Once a day | Once a year | *Once an hour | Once a week
exercise: Sam earns an hourly rate of £10 and works 3 hours. How much does he earn in total? | £300 | £13 | *£30 | £7
test: «A salary is yearly pay; an hourly rate is pay for each hour worked.» Which word means pay for each hour? | Yearly pay | Salary | Career | *Hourly rate
test: Priya earns £8 an hour and works 4 hours. What is her total pay? | £84 | £12 | *£32 | £24
exam: Maya is paid an hourly rate of £6 for 5 hours. What does she earn? | *£30 | £5 | £11 | £56
